Older bundled libc++ (Android NDK r25, still used for API < 21 targets since
newer NDKs dropped that support -- see arm-neon-android-19.cmake) predates
the std::contiguous_iterator concept even though it has the rest of C++20
<concepts>/<iterator>. Drop the constraint on these abbreviated-template
parameters -- it was only a compile-time contract, every call site already
passes a contiguous iterator (raw pointer / std::vector::iterator), so
behavior is unaffected.

